WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.780
Though 2018's Halloween recaptures the stripped-down
aesthetics of Carpenter's original vision,

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:10.060
there's still a handful of treats scattered
among its tricks, waiting to be found by sharp-eyed

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:10.700
fans.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:14.860
Come along with us as we give you a brief
rundown of the secrets hiding in Halloween's

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.360
shadows.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.000
Just watch out for the boogeyman… and spoilers.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.640
And spoilers...

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:23.070
Understandably, the focus of much of Halloween's
hype has been on Jamie Lee Curtis and the

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.140
return of the role that made her famous, Laurie
Strode.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.580
Curtis' 1978 performance remains iconic in
the annals of horror history, earning her

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.519
the lingering title of "Scream Queen."

00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:37.329
She played Laurie again across three other
decades, starring in 1981's Halloween II,

00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:41.539
1998's Halloween H20, and 2002's Halloween:
Resurrection.

00:00:41.539 --> 00:00:45.530
She even lent her voice to Halloween III:
Season of the Witch, the unrelated stand-alone

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:47.780
entry in which she can be heard as an announcer.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:55.440
"Curfew, curfew, all residents of Santa Mira
please clear the streets."

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.999
However, while those previous sequels tended
to leave Laurie sidelined in a hospital bed

00:00:59.999 --> 00:01:05.119
or killed off after a glorified cameo, the
2018 film is fully dedicated to her story,

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
exploring the trauma that has affected her
life and her family.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.120
Less obvious are some other returning performers
joining Curtis.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.180
Michael Myers was played by two different
actors in Carpenter's film - Nick Castle was

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:18.810
the man behind the mask, while Tony Moran
portrayed the killer for the single scene

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.220
in which his face can be glimpsed.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.880
Castle is back this time around, sharing the
role of Michael with newcomer James Jude Courtney.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.900
The new Halloween takes us back to the fictional
town of Haddonfield, Illinois, the small community

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.380
once rocked by Michael Myers' original murders.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.540
While the story keeps a tight focus on Laurie,
her daughter Karen, and her granddaughter

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:40.880
Allyson, the filmmakers nonetheless made sure
to include a few nods to the continuing history

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.200
of the town around them.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.340
The original Halloween was shot during the
summer in California.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.409
Grappling with a very modest budget, Carpenter's
crew had to simulate a Midwestern autumn by

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:53.540
spreading dead leaves on the ground, despite
the trees visibly blooming in several shots.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:58.260
The new movie, shot in South Carolina in the
winter, recreates this unsettling juxtaposition

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:02.310
during an early scene in which Allyson and
her friends stroll down Haddonfield's leaf-strewn

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.900
sidewalks under green foliage.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.550
Beyond the visuals, citizens are name-checked
too, with Allyson's boyfriend Cameron Elam

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:13.500
established as the son of Lonnie Elam, a trouble-making
classmate of young Tommy Doyle in 1978.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.520
In addition to set dressing and name-drops,
David Gordon Green and Danny McBride peppered

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:22.000
their new Halloween with a number of cinematic
allusions to its predecessor.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.600
From in-jokes and references to inversions
and reversals, it will be impossible for longtime

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:31.030
Halloween fans to watch this new take without
feeling a certain sense of déjà vu.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:34.890
This is obvious right from the opening titles,
which revive the jack-o-lantern that kicked

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:35.860
off the first movie.

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:40.580
Michael's 2018 hospital escape mirrors his
first, with white-gowned mental patients wandering

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:42.420
eerily by the glow of car headlights.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:46.260
Later, a familiar playground rhyme echoes
during the trick-or-treat sequence.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:50.110
The real fun begins, though, when Laurie herself
takes the place of Michael in a number of

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:54.560
familiar moments, particularly the climactic
balcony fall and subsequent disappearance.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.190
Her face also looms in the darkness behind
him at one point, just as he had loomed behind

00:02:59.190 --> 00:02:59.680
her.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.840
"Happy Halloween Michael.”

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:06.560
In the end, the fire that at last consumes
the Shape also burns a dollhouse, which bears

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:09.160
a passing resemblance to the original Myers
home.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.360
While the new movie ignores all the sequels
that preceded it, McBride and Green still

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:16.610
set out with an intention to pay tribute to
every Halloween movie.

00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:21.140
Their film states that Michael has been in
custody ever since that fateful night in 1978,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.460
making it clear that none of his later shenanigans
ever happened in its world.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:29.260
However, winks and nods abound to console
fans who might be miffed about this new timeline.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.590
1981's Halloween II revealed that Laurie and
Michael were siblings, suggesting that his

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.520
killing spree was somehow motivated by his
own bloodline.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.900
Further sequels took this concept further,
sending the Shape after more relatives and

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:50.100
proposing an ancient curse as his motivation.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.920
The new movie has Allyson quickly dispel the
notion of Laurie and Michael being sister

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:54.600
and brother.

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:57.920
"Wasn't it her brother who murdered all those
babysitters?”

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.430
“No, it was not her brother.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:00.620
That's something that people made up."

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:05.520
More subtle sequel references include a glimpse
at Halloween III's sinister masks, a gas station

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.320
bearing a strong resemblance to a set from
The Return of Michael Myers, and a public

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.720
restroom setting similar to a scene in H20.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.380
Donald Pleasence was one of the few consistent
mainstays of the Halloween sequels, playing

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:18.860
Dr. Sam Loomis in five films before his death.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.300
Acting as something of a Van Helsing to Michael's
Dracula, Loomis dedicated his entire life

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:26.780
to stopping his famous patient, even when
no one believed him about the danger they

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:27.420
were in.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:31.760
In the first movie, he sums up the Shape's
unknowable motivations as succinctly as possible:

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:37.220
"I realized that what was living behind that
boy's eyes was purely and simply evil."

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.220
The new movie pays rather subtle but brilliant
homage to this idea.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:46.160
Though the 2018 Halloween takes place in a
timeline where Michael never escaped again

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:50.780
during the late Loomis' lifetime, his dedication
still plays a major role, and the character

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:53.570
even makes a cassette tape cameo via a Pleasence
soundalike.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:58.220
We are introduced to a man dubbed "the new
Loomis" by Laurie, Dr. Sartain, whose unhealthy

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:02.360
obsession with understanding Michael's motivations
leads him to betray the heroes towards the

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:03.260
film's climax.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:07.940
In the end, the bad doctor learns that what
Laurie and Loomis have always said is true:

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.600
there's no reasoning with pure evil.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.680
"It was the boogeyman.”

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.640
“As a matter of fact, it was."

